cartridges on a socket: run in the back, handle the events

Usage: zirkle [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  daemon  
  launch  Start the harness proxy and run an agent against it: `zirkle launch claude -- -p hi`
  mcp     Serve the profile's tools to an MCP client over this terminal's stdio: `claude mcp add zirkle -- zirkle mcp`
  run     Load a profile, call one service in the foreground, and dispose it
  send    
  tail    
  call    Call a provided key with one JSON argument and print the reply
  reload  
  status  
  debug   Enter, leave or report debug mode on the running host: `zirkle debug on`
  socket  
  list    Cartridges of the profile and what each one needs, resolved to its provider
  verify  Load the profile and run every contract its cartridges declare
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --dir <DIR>          Directory containing bundled cartridges (each with cartridge.json)
      --profile <PROFILE>  Profile name under `.zirkle/`, or an absolute profile directory (default `default`; `proxy` for launch)
      --yolo               Automatic execution: bypass tool policy and skip resolver provenance recording
  -h, --help               Print help
